From d87bdce46d8dae7d0dfc6a19061f27c62b71fcf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:02:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] firmware: qcom: tzmem: disable SHM Bridge on Galaxy A70

The Galaxy A70 secure firmware reports SHM Bridge support, but its ADSP PAS init-image request subsequently fails with -EINVAL. The working downstream kernel does not enable SHM Bridge.

Use the generic TZ memory backend only on this machine. Other SM6150 and QCS615 devices may ship different secure firmware and should not be blacklisted without independent evidence.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
index f926c1f64..8bfe4e5e7 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ static const char *const qcom_tzmem_blacklist[] = {
 	"qcom,sc8180x",
 	"qcom,sdm670", /* failure in GPU firmware loading */
 	"qcom,sdm845", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
+	"samsung,a70q", /* failure in ADSP firmware loading */
 	"qcom,sm7150", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
 	"qcom,sm8150", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
 	NULL
